# --- FINAL SCORE + GRADE OUTPUTS: DELIBERATELY IN GIT (Principal, 2026-08-07) ---
# `*.csv` above excludes everything by default, which is right for working files but wrong for the
# finished scores. Anyone handed the SG_NDPMS_TEMP1 skill must get the stock scores and the MF grades
# WITHOUT re-running the pipeline -- that was the whole point of the handover. These are outputs, not
# inputs: small (~1.6 MB total), regenerated on the Apr/Oct cadence, and useless to recompute by hand.
# Negations must be listed file by file; a blanket `!*.csv` would drag every working file back in.
!Shreyas_Ionic_AMC/04_RND_LAB/STOCK_SCORECARD_750/results/full750_scored.csv
!Shreyas_Ionic_AMC/04_RND_LAB/STOCK_SCORECARD_750/results/full750_scored_v3.csv
!Shreyas_Ionic_AMC/04_RND_LAB/STOCK_SCORECARD_750/results/portfolio_quant.csv
!Shreyas_Ionic_AMC/04_RND_LAB/STOCK_SCORECARD_750/results/EARNINGS_QUALITY.csv
!Shreyas_Ionic_AMC/03_RESEARCH_DESK/MF_RECOMMENDATIONS/**/QFRA1_all_categories.csv
!Shreyas_Ionic_AMC/03_RESEARCH_DESK/MF_RECOMMENDATIONS/**/QFRA2_verdicts.csv
!Shreyas_Ionic_AMC/03_RESEARCH_DESK/MF_RECOMMENDATIONS/**/QFRA2_current_asof_*.csv
# Still excluded on purpose -- the WORKING data behind those scores, which nobody should need:
#   datasets/screener_deep/*.parquet   raw financials  |  ALPHA_RANKER/data/prices/  price panels
#   MF_RECOMMENDATIONS/**/fund_daily.csv, bench.csv, codes.csv, wb_tail.csv, results_asof_*.csv
# Consequence, stated so it is not a surprise: with the scores but not the working data you can BUILD
# decks and READ scores, but you cannot RE-RUN the scoring chain (it needs the screener parquets and
# the price panel) or any backtest. Ask the Principal if you need to regenerate rather than consume.

